{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "title": "Dataset-wise TD-Tree 32T baseline comparison",
  "as_of": "2026-07-29",
  "description": "Protocol-corrected comparison: Original (TD-Tree) CPU32 reads each unfiltered graph, while Ours CPU32, Ours+Gopher CPU32, and Ours+Gopher-GPU read the corresponding supplied prefiltered graph.",
  "repeats": 5,
  "timeout_seconds": 900,
  "methodology": {
    "primary_metric": "Median cold-process online wall time over five isolated, interleaved repetitions. Original includes raw-file loading and TD-Tree preprocessing; proposed methods load a precomputed filtered file.",
    "semantic_group": "All four configurations require at least k consecutive common snapshots. The TD-Tree baseline therefore uses the explicit consecutive compatibility mode, not the 2022 paper's cardinality default.",
    "workload": "Each dataset uses the same dataset-specific directed path query across algorithms, with three edges, k=3, stable-ID label mode, label seed 42, and count-only output.",
    "cpu_threads": "All CPU configurations request 32 threads and are pinned to logical CPUs 0-31. TD-Tree and Ours use true count-only root-task workers; Ours+Gopher uses bounded dynamic-prefix workers.",
    "gpu": "Ours+Gopher-GPU uses the resident-continuation Candidate-DAG executor on the Radeon 8060S through WSL /dev/dxg. It has no silent CPU fallback and no CPU dependency-key runtime memo tables.",
    "correctness": "Every configuration must finish every repetition, remain count-stable, and agree on match count within each dataset. Stable-ID labeling is required because the source graphs have no native vertex labels and raw/filtered vertex universes differ.",
    "input_protocol": "Original (TD-Tree) consumes the file without _filtered. Ours, Ours+Gopher, and Ours+Gopher-GPU consume the paired _filtered file. The runner records and validates the resolved per-algorithm path and SHA-256.",
    "timing_boundary": "This is the user-requested precomputed-filter online comparison. Section 4.1/4.3 of 260408_cdh.pdf says paper-style total time includes filtering construction; therefore these medians must not be described as a numerical replication of that paper's end-to-end figure.",
    "output_boundary": "Count-only suppresses materialization of every mapping to a large text file; it does not mean that no matches were found."
  },
